# --------------------------------------------------
# Development container versions and manual update guide.
#
# This file pins the Debian snapshot, system packages, and downloaded tools
# installed directly by the development-container Dockerfile. Debian packages
# move with their snapshot, not independently through a latest-version feed.
#
# Run commands from the repository root in a trusted Linux maintenance workspace.
# The configured devcontainer supplies the required tools. Docker must be running
# and downloads require network access. Use a disposable worktree for updates
# because a failed refresh can leave some files updated and others unchanged.
#
# 1. Choose the versions to change
#    Edit exact tool pins in mise.toml and Feature options in devcontainer.json.
#    Update the base-image or frontend tag and digest together in Dockerfile.
#    Node and pnpm declarations in package.json are derived from mise.toml by
#    the refresh command, so do not update those declarations independently.
#
# 2. If changing the mise bootstrap, use the signed updater
#    Replace VERSION with the release number without a leading v. This updates
#    MISE_VERSION, both committed Linux hashes, mise's minimum version and the
#    CI bootstrap pin together. Do not paste replacement hashes by hand.
#    bash scripts/linux/commands/devcontainer/devcontainer-update.sh --mise VERSION
#
# 3. Refresh the complete dependency set and check drift
#    This verifies the bootstrap, regenerates locks for both Linux platforms,
#    refreshes native npm/Python dependency graphs and advances the Debian
#    snapshot to a recent UTC date with a seven-day delay. Exact tool pins stay
#    fixed. Debian package versions below are resolved as one matching set for
#    amd64 and arm64 rather than guessed or updated independently.
#    bash scripts/linux/commands/devcontainer/devcontainer-update.sh --refresh
#
#    To select a specific Debian snapshot instead, run this after the refresh.
#    Replace YYYYMMDD with the chosen UTC date. The resolver updates the snapshot
#    and every Debian package pin together without installing those packages.
#    It rejects backwards dates and versions that differ between architectures.
#    node scripts/node/bin/update-debian-snapshot.js YYYYMMDDT000000Z
#
#    For lock regeneration only, without advancing the snapshot or deliberately
#    bumping native transitive dependencies, use the following instead of refresh.
#    This does not synchronize changed Node/pnpm declarations in package.json.
#    bash scripts/linux/commands/devcontainer/devcontainer-update.sh --locks
#
# 4. Review and test the candidate before rebuilding your working container
#    git diff -- .devcontainer mise.toml mise.lock .mise package.json pnpm-lock.yaml .github/actions/setup-node-deps/action.yml
#    pnpm run test:devcontainer:inputs
#    pnpm run test:devcontainer
#    pnpm run devcontainer:scan
#
#    The smoke test builds a disposable container and verifies its lifecycle.
#    The security scan is a separate gate. Do not treat startup as a scan pass.
#    Commit the reviewed pins and generated locks together. Never edit native
#    lock sidecars by hand because mise owns their contents and recorded hashes.
#
# 5. Rebuild the working container to install the reviewed versions
#    This replaces the existing workspace container, so save your work first.
#    pnpm run devcontainer:rebuild
#
#    To check inputs later without changing files, use the following command.
#    The available mise executable must satisfy the committed minimum version.
#    If the bootstrap changed, use the rebuilt container or the new pinned mise.
#    bash scripts/linux/commands/devcontainer/devcontainer-update.sh --check
# --------------------------------------------------

# --------------------------------------------------
# Development-container version pins.
#
# Pins the Debian snapshot, direct system packages and mise bootstrap.
# Update Debian packages together with their snapshot, not independently.
# Tool pins belong in mise.toml and Feature options in devcontainer.json.
#
# Run updates from the repository root in a trusted disposable worktree.
# The devcontainer provides the tools. Updates require network access.
#
# Update the signed mise bootstrap, replacing VERSION with the release number
# bash scripts/linux/commands/devcontainer/devcontainer-update.sh --mise VERSION
#
# Refresh the snapshot, coupled declarations and dependency locks
# bash scripts/linux/commands/devcontainer/devcontainer-update.sh --refresh
#
# Check without changing files
# bash scripts/linux/commands/devcontainer/devcontainer-update.sh --check
#
# Review the diff, test and scan before rebuilding your working container.
# See TODO.md for the complete update and rebuild workflow.
# --------------------------------------------------

DEBIAN_SNAPSHOT=20260824T000000Z
CMARK_GFM_VERSION=0.29.0.gfm.6-6
CURL_VERSION=7.88.1-10+deb12u15
GAWK_VERSION=1:5.2.1-2
GIT_LFS_VERSION=3.3.0-1+deb12u1
PYTHON_VENV_VERSION=3.11.2-1+b1
JQ_VERSION=1.6-2.1+deb12u2
YQ_VERSION=3.1.0-3
MISE_VERSION=2026.9.18
